+# NUI v8 — Agent Interoperability & Visual Media Intelligence Design
+
+## Problem
+
+NUI v7 can route authority, compile concrete craft decisions and inspect rendered perception, but two gaps remain. First, agents use heterogeneous discovery/permission surfaces; copying NUI into each host would fork the corpus and drift. Second, visually ambitious UI can remain generic by substituting high-salience abstract geometry for subject-native evidence, then pass ordinary runtime/aesthetic checks.
+
+## Architecture
+
+V8 adds four bounded planes rather than a parallel design system: (1) portable agent discovery over one canonical graph, (2) external-skill supply-chain trust, (3) visual-media representation/provenance, and (4) creative-toolchain orchestration plus rendered integration. Eight decision owners are added only where no existing owner has the boundary.
+
+## Invariants
+
+- Host adapters are thin pointers. Access/transport cannot raise design authority or permissions.
+- External skills remain advisory until immutable snapshot, license, transitive resources and capability envelope are reviewed.
+- Geometry is legal when it earns semantic/compositional value; shape substitution is the failure mode.
+- Search providers are discovery surfaces, never blanket asset licenses.
+- Creative tools own execution operations, not product truth, rights truth or completion.
+- Material media must be re-observed inside responsive/temporal UI states.
+- Every new skill participates in the full-graph five-anchor depth lock and falsification/recovery contract.
+
+## Verification
+
+V8 adds four adversarial planes (agent interoperability, external skill trust, visual media, creative toolchain), eight cases each. Repository validation checks all registries, bridges, schemas, graph/manifest parity, depth saturation and 32 cases. Task completion inherits v7 and blocks unresolved trust/provenance/shape/integration conditions.
+
+## Copyright boundary
+
+NUI stores links, evidence and independently written mechanism summaries by default. Copying/vendoring is an explicit adoption mode that requires exact rights. External visual assets are admitted at asset granularity with creator/source/license/transform lineage. Generated media is recorded as generated and is not treated as factual or automatically rights-clear.
